Package: svylearn
Title: Design-Consistent Statistical Learning, Calibration, and Inference
    for Complex Surveys
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(person("Sunday A.", "Adetunji", email = "sundayadetunjisa@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(affiliation = "Oregon State University")),
    person("Oluwatimileyin A.", "Adetunji", email = "eniola16.to@gmail.com", role = "aut",
    comment = c(affiliation = "Bowen University")))
Description: Combines whole-cluster resampling, training-fold weighted
    preprocessing, nested tuning, probability recalibration and design-based
    evaluation for binary, continuous, count and multiclass outcomes in
    cross-sectional and longitudinal probability samples. Survey design
    inference is delegated to the 'survey' package. Optional learner adapters
    are loaded only when requested. Includes weighted principal components,
    time-eligible trajectory features, population utility, calibration,
    transport-balance, sensitivity and conformal evaluation diagnostics.
    Sequential retention models can be refitted inside nested validation
    to construct attrition weights from baseline panel rosters.
    Implements reusable elements of the
    workflow described by Adetunji et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.29244/currbiomed.5.1.7>.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, utils, graphics, splines
Suggests: survey, glmnet, ranger, xgboost, nnet, testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown
